PN,30807
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786621676
OL,3,CNurses collapsing on shift in
OL,4,C'unbearably hot' hospitals during
OL,5,Cheatwave
OL,7,FThe NHS has been ordered by health
OL,8,Fsecretary Yvette Cooper to prepare for
OL,9,Fthe effects of heatwaves each year in
OL,10,Fthe same way that it plans for winter.
OL,12,FEarlier this year the Climate Change
OL,13,FCommittee of MPs said that the
OL,14,Fgovernment should ensure cooling
OL,15,Fmeasures are installed in hospitals
OL,16,Fand care homes by 2035, ranging from
OL,17,Fshading through to air conditioning.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30808
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786621676
OL,3,CNurses collapsing on shift in
OL,4,C'unbearably hot' hospitals during
OL,5,Cheatwave
OL,7,FRuth Wilkinson, head of policy at the
OL,8,FInstitution of Occupational Safety and
OL,9,FHealth, said indoor workers, like
OL,10,Fnurses, can find work in extreme heat
OL,11,Fjust as challenging as outdoor workers.
OL,13,F"This can be due to poor ventilation,
OL,14,Flack of cooling infrastructure, and
OL,15,Foutdated building designs that leave
OL,16,Fthem to cope in stifling conditions,"
OL,17,FWilkinson said.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30809
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786621676
OL,3,CNurses collapsing on shift in
OL,4,C'unbearably hot' hospitals during
OL,5,Cheatwave
OL,7,F"Heat stress can make it harder for
OL,8,Fpeople to work safely and effectively.
OL,9,FWhen it's too hot, the body has to
OL,10,Fwork harder to stay cool, which can
OL,11,Flead to health problems like
OL,12,Fdehydration, heat exhaustion, or even
OL,13,Fheat stroke.
OL,15,F"Employers can take proactive steps to
OL,16,Fmanage these risks and support
OL,17,Fworkers. These can include adjusting
OL,18,Fwork hours, providing cooling
OL,19,Fstations, and encouraging hydration."
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30810
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786621676
OL,3,CNurses collapsing on shift in
OL,4,C'unbearably hot' hospitals during
OL,5,Cheatwave
OL,7,FHealth Secretary Yvette Cooper said:
OL,8,F"The extreme heat is hitting public
OL,9,Fhealth and our NHS.
OL,11,F"Across the NHS and social care, staff
OL,12,Fare doing a remarkable job to respond
OL,13,Fto rising A&E attendances and
OL,14,Fambulance call-outs, heat problems
OL,15,Famongst the elderly and difficult
OL,16,Fworking conditions. I want to thank
OL,17,Fthem for all their work.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30811
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786621676
OL,3,CNurses collapsing on shift in
OL,4,C'unbearably hot' hospitals during
OL,5,Cheatwave
OL,7,F"But I have also been clear that the
OL,8,FNHS now needs to plan for summer
OL,9,Fpressures in the way we currently plan
OL,10,Ffor winter pressures. That includes
OL,11,Fmaking sure buildings are more
OL,12,Fresilient in these new extreme heat
OL,13,Fconditions as well as responding to
OL,14,Fadditional patient needs."
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
